<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mau Mau rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1952–1960</span> · Also known as Mau Mau uprising, Kenya Emergency</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mau Mau rebellion was an armed uprising in colonial Kenya, mainly among the Kikuyu, against British rule and European settlement on African land. The British declared a state of emergency in 1952, detained tens of thousands in camps and killed many thousands of suspected rebels. The emergency ended in 1960, and Kenya became independent in 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mau-mau-rebellion.jpg" alt="Mau Mau rebellion" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministry of Defence POST-1945 OFFICIAL COLLECTION · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KAR_Mau_Mau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
